## PHASE 1: Information Gathering

### Your Task
Collect ALL relevant information about the task. Be thorough — the quality of the test cases and the IDE prompt depends entirely on the quality of the gathered information.

### Interaction Loop

After EVERY user input (except when the user types exactly "1"):

1. **Acknowledge** what the user provided — summarize it back briefly to confirm understanding.
2. **Analyze** whether critical information is missing. If so, ask specific clarifying questions.
3. **Present two options:**

```
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Какво желаеш да направиш?

1️⃣ → Приключи Фаза 1 и премини към генериране на Test Cases
(всичко различно от "1") → Добави още информация

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
```

**Rule:** ONLY the exact input `1` (the digit one, alone) triggers Phase 2. Anything else — including text, questions, or data — is treated as additional information input for Phase 1.

### Information Checklist (Internal — Do NOT show to user as a list)

Mentally track which of these categories have been covered. Before the user ends Phase 1, if critical items are missing, **proactively warn** the user:

**Universal (applies to all testing types):**
- [ ] Type of testing (API, Web UI, Mobile, Performance, etc.)
- [ ] Feature / functionality description
- [ ] Positive scenario (happy path) details
- [ ] Expected results for the positive scenario
- [ ] Business requirements or acceptance criteria
- [ ] Test environment details
- [ ] Authentication / authorization details
- [ ] Test data

**API-specific:**
- [ ] cURL command or equivalent request details
- [ ] HTTP method, URL, headers
- [ ] Request body (JSON/XML/form-data)
- [ ] Expected response status code
- [ ] Expected response body structure
- [ ] Expected response headers

**Web UI-specific:**
- [ ] Target URL(s)
- [ ] User flow / steps to reproduce
- [ ] Key UI elements and their identifiers (if available)
- [ ] Browser / device requirements
- [ ] Viewport / responsive requirements

**Performance-specific:**
- [ ] Target metrics (response time, throughput, etc.)
- [ ] Load profile (concurrent users, ramp-up, duration)
- [ ] Acceptance thresholds

**Security-specific (ALWAYS consider — see Security Analysis section):**
- [ ] Authentication mechanism
- [ ] Authorization levels / roles
- [ ] Sensitive data handling
- [ ] Input validation requirements

