## PHASE 2: Test Case Generation

### Step 2.1: Format Selection

Present these 4 format options:

```
Избери формат за Test Cases:

1️⃣ Класически формат
   Test Case ID: TC-{number}
   Title: {description}
   Preconditions: {setup required}
   Test Steps:
     1. {step}
     2. {step}
   Expected Result: {what should occur}
   Priority: {High/Medium/Low}

2️⃣ BDD формат (Given-When-Then)
   Scenario: {description}
   Given {precondition}
   When {action}
   Then {expected outcome}

3️⃣ Табличен формат
   | TC ID | Description | Steps/Input | Expected Result | Priority |

4️⃣ Потребителски формат
   Сподели своя шаблон и ще го следвам.
```

### Step 2.2: Test Case Generation

Generate test cases organized by sections. Apply ONLY the sections relevant to the type of testing identified in Phase 1. Each task gets a **security analysis** regardless of type.

**IMPORTANT RULES:**
- Each test case tests ONE thing only.
- Number all test cases sequentially across all sections.
- The FIRST test case is always the positive (happy path) scenario.
- Mark priority for each test case: `[High]`, `[Medium]`, or `[Low]`.

---

### UNIVERSAL SECTIONS (Apply to ALL types of testing)

#### SECTION U1: Positive Test Case (Happy Path)

Always generate exactly ONE positive test case based on the provided information.

**Title format:** `1. [Positive Test Case] [High] {User-provided name or default based on context}`

Examples:
- API: `1. [Positive Test Case] [High] Successful POST request to /api/users`
- Web UI: `1. [Positive Test Case] [High] Successful user login with valid credentials`
- Performance: `1. [Positive Test Case] [High] Response time within SLA under normal load`

---

